,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Mar–May in Auckland has warmed by about 0.15 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1 °C in all, with the coldest days warming fastest, so cold extremes are becoming rarer. El Niño has no identifiable effect on Mar–May temperature. Mar–May rainfall has fallen by about 5% per decade. El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a drier season with less intense heavy-rain days, and this year's shift is substantial. Relative humidity has fallen by about 0.3 points per decade, roughly 2 points since 1951; because warmer air holds more moisture, this does not necessarily mean the air is drier. For Mar–May 2027, the temperature odds are close to even; a drier-than-normal season is more likely than not (about 60%). The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":16.9334,"trend_per_decade":0.127,"trend_p":0.0002,"trend_total_since_1951":0.9525,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.0805,"enso_p":0.2957,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","survives_fdr":false,"fraction_explained":0.0152,"intrinsic_sd":0.6078,"effect_this_season":-0.1618,"effect_ratio":0.2662,"size":"Noticeable","size_typical_el_nino":"Negligible","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":null,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.1743,"forecast_mean":17.1077,"forecast_sd":0.6517,"p_below":0.3579,"p_near":0.2707,"p_above":0.3713,"forecast_words":"Near-equal odds of below, near and above normal","within_record":false,"enso_effect_shrunk_per_degC":-0.0639,"shrink_factor":0.7943,"effect_this_season_raw":-0.2037,"trend_part_2027":0.3361,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":-12.7373,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.1563,"trend_p